event: tool_result
data: {"content":"## Slash commands\n\n### Runnable with \"run\"\n\n- caveman [lite|full|ultra] — Shorter answers to cut output tokens\n- caveman-finish — Return to normal output length\n- ponytail [lite|full|ultra|off] — Toggle lazy-senior-dev mode\n- superpowers [objective] — Enable the disciplined plan-first, verify-always workflow\n- learning [focus] — Enable learner mode: read the KB more and document discoveries\n- improve-agents-md [guidance] — Create or reinforce AGENTS.md with the mandatory agent rules\n- vulnhunt [scope] — Adversarial security audit from attacker input to sinks\n- vulnhunter-fix [finding] — Test-driven remediation of confirmed vulnerabilities\n- vulnhunt-fix-verify [findings] — Independent read-only verification of claimed security fixes\n\n### User-only\n\n- summarize — Alias for /compact (compaction cannot run inside an active turn)\n- db-compact — Compact the database (VACUUM) and reclaim free space (database maintenance is triggered by the user)\n- learning-finish — Consolidate what was learned into KB/memory and return to normal mode (the closing turn is user-driven so the mode clears only on success)\n- goal — Start goal mode with a persistent objective (goal mode is started by the user)\n- goal-status — Show the status of the current goal (goal mode is started by the user)\n- superpowers-finish — Verify and close the active Superpowers workflow, then return to normal mode (the closing turn is user-driven so the mode clears only on success)\n- autopilot — Alias for /goal (goal mode is started by the user)\n- goal-cancel — Cancel the current goal execution (goal mode is started by the user)\n- compact — Create a manual compact summary for the current session (compaction cannot run inside an active turn)\n","is_error":false,"kind":"other","locations":null,"name":"pando_setup","raw_output":{"output":"## Slash commands\n\n### Runnable with \"run\"\n\n- caveman [lite|full|ultra] — Shorter answers to cut output tokens\n- caveman-finish — Return to normal output length\n- ponytail [lite|full|ultra|off] — Toggle lazy-senior-dev mode\n- superpowers [objective] — Enable the disciplined plan-first, verify-always workflow\n- learning [focus] — Enable learner mode: read the KB more and document discoveries\n- improve-agents-md [guidance] — Create or reinforce AGENTS.md with the mandatory agent rules\n- vulnhunt [scope] — Adversarial security audit from attacker input to sinks\n- vulnhunter-fix [finding] — Test-driven remediation of confirmed vulnerabilities\n- vulnhunt-fix-verify [findings] — Independent read-only verification of claimed security fixes\n\n### User-only\n\n- summarize — Alias for /compact (compaction cannot run inside an active turn)\n- db-compact — Compact the database (VACUUM) and reclaim free space (database maintenance is triggered by the user)\n- learning-finish — Consolidate what was learned into KB/memory and return to normal mode (the closing turn is user-driven so the mode clears only on success)\n- goal — Start goal mode with a persistent objective (goal mode is started by the user)\n- goal-status — Show the status of the current goal (goal mode is started by the user)\n- superpowers-finish — Verify and close the active Superpowers workflow, then return to normal mode (the closing turn is user-driven so the mode clears only on success)\n- autopilot — Alias for /goal (goal mode is started by the user)\n- goal-cancel — Cancel the current goal execution (goal mode is started by the user)\n- compact — Create a manual compact summary for the current session (compaction cannot run inside an active turn)\n"},"status":"completed","title":"pando_setup","tool_call_id":"call_uuwzVV7E1JbodJw57E1kh3HG"}

